event: content_block_start
data: {"type":"content_block_start","index":1,"content_block":{"type":"web_search_tool_result","tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_is_00_99d9c5ad6bc642a0807e94010cbf007a","content":[{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Eiffel Tower","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffel_Tower","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"2001-03-01T00:00:00+00:00","snippet":"\nTower in Paris, France\n\nThis article is about the landmark in Paris, France. For other uses, see Eiffel Tower (disambiguation).\n\n\"300-metre tower\" and \"Tour Eiffel\" redirect here. For other tall towers, see List of tallest towers. For other uses, see Tour Eiffel (disambiguation).\n\nEiffel Tower \n\nTour Eiffel (French)\n\n\n \n\n\nSeen from the Champ de Mars, 2009\n\n\nMap\n\nInteractive","site_name":"Wikipedia","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/wikipedia.org","image_url":"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Tour_Eiffel_Wikimedia_Commons_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Tour_Eiffel_Wikimedia_Commons_%28cropped%29.jpg"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Eiffel Tower","url":"https://www.heritage.site/europe/france/ile-de-france/paris/eiffel-tower","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null,"snippet":"\n\nEiffel Tower\n\nEiffel Tower - Credit: Wikimedia Commons\n\nThe Eiffel Tower ( ; ) is a wrought-iron lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower from 1887 to 1889. Read more on Wikipedia\n\n- type: building\n- date from: 1889\n- official website: toureiffel.paris/en\n","site_name":null,"site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/heritage.site","image_url":"https://www.heritage.site/assets/images/1280px/8/n/8/1280px-Tour_Eiffel_Wikimedia_Commons_(cropped).jpg.08n8ecfa4cjtbwj1jufqghehimztu1s7t.webp"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Carleton College","url":"https://serc.carleton.edu/details/images/33372.html","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null,"snippet":"SERC Media\n\nEiffel Tower\n\n\nView Original Image at Full Size\n\nThe Eiffel Tower, seen from the champ de Mars, Paris, France\n\nOriginally uploaded in Cutting Edge:Topics:Rates and Time.\n\nImage 33372 is a 1023 by 553 pixel JPEG\n\nUploaded: May7 12\n\nLast Modified: 2012-05-07 16:59:40\n\nPermanent URL: https://serc.carleton.edu/download/images/","site_name":"Carleton College","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/carleton.edu","image_url":"https://serc.carleton.edu/images/NAGTWorkshops/time/eiffel_tower_351.jpg"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Eiffel Tower","url":"https://help.g2rail.com/poi/W__5013364","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null,"snippet":"\n## Paris, France\n\n\nThe Eiffel Tower is a wrought iron lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower. Constructed from 1887–89 as the entrance to the 1889 World's Fair, it was initially criticized by some of France's leading artists and intellectuals for its design, but it has become a global cultural icon of France and one of the most recogn","site_name":"G2Rail","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/g2rail.com","image_url":"https://sematicweb.detie.cn/content/W__5013364__6ac2c08af632.jpg"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Places like Eiffel Tower","url":"https://tastedive.com/places/like/eiffel-tower","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null,"snippet":"places\n\nHistorical Landmark\n\nTourist Attraction\n\nPlace\n\n\n## Eiffel Tower\n\nAv. Gustave Eiffel 75007 Paris France\n\n3.9/5\n\nGustave Eiffel's iconic, wrought-iron 1889 tower, with steps and elevators to observation decks.\n\nPicture of a place: Eiffel Tower\n\nFilter by:\n\n## Cross-category suggestions\n\nFilter by:\n\nFilter by:\n\nFilter by:\n\nFilter by:\n\nFilter by:\n\nFilter by","site_name":"TasteDive","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/tastedive.com","image_url":"https://images.qloo.com/i/5947d28c-2684-41eb-9d8b-f1ea26ab7a77-400x300-outside.webp"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"","url":"https://touradvice.info/france/paris/eiffeltower.html","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null,"snippet":"www.touradvice.info\n\nTravel and Vacation Advice\n\nEiffel Tower\n\n\nEiffel tower\n\n\nEiffel Tower is in Paris. Its height is 1063 feet. It was inaugurated on 31st March, 1889. It is the highest iron tower in the world.\n\nEiffel Tower was not built as a permanent monument. It was built as a temporary monument. Now, this is one of the wonders of the world. In 1889, there","site_name":null,"site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/touradvice.info","image_url":"https://touradvice.info/images/eiffel%20tower.jpg"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"World's most visited monument with an entrance fee: The Eiffel Tower","url":"https://www.worldrecordacademy.org/2023/8/world-s-most-visited-monument-with-an-entrance-fee-the-eiffel-tower-423322","encrypted_content":"","page_age":"2023-08-15T00:00:00+00:00","snippet":"Blog Post\n\n\nAug 15, 2023\n\nWorld's most visited monument with an entrance fee: The Eiffel Tower\n\nParis, France--The Eiffel Tower, nicknamed \"La dame de fer\" (French for \"Iron Lady\"), a wrought-iron lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France, was named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower; named part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site, the tower received","site_name":"World Record Academy","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/worldrecordacademy.org","image_url":"https://irp.cdn-website.com/08d31351/dms3rep/multi/423322-b1-most-visited-monument-eiffel-tower.jpg"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"巴黎鐵塔","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230328121359/https://zh-yue.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%B7%B4%E9%BB%8E%E9%90%B5%E5%A1%94","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null,"snippet":"COLLECTED BY\n\nCollection: Common Crawl\n\nWeb crawl data from Common Crawl.\n\nTIMESTAMPS\n\nThe Wayback Machine - https://web.archive.org/web/20230328121359/https://zh-yue.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E5%B7%B4%E9%BB%8E%E9%90%B5%E5%A1%94\n\n\n出自維基百科，自由嘅百科全書\n\n跳去導覽 跳去搵嘢\n\n |","site_name":"Wayback Machine","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/archive.org","image_url":"http://web.archive.org/web/20230328121359im_/https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Tour_Eiffel_Wikimedia_Commons.jpg/330px-Tour_Eiffel_Wikimedia_Commons.jpg"},{"type":"web_search_result","title":"Where in the World quiz – the answers","url":"https://joethecockershikes.com/2023/11/29/where-in-the-world-quiz-the-answers/","encrypted_content":"","page_age":null,"snippet":"Skip to content\n\n\nWe hope that you spotted where the photographs were taken. The answers are below 👍🐾🐾\n\n1. Machu Picchu, Peru\n\n\n2. Angkor Wat, Cambodia\n\n\n3. Eifel Tower, Paris, France\n\n\n4. John Lennon Memorial, Strawberry Field, Central Park in New York\n\n\n5. Mt. Rushmore, South Dakota, USA\n\n\n6. The Sphinx, Giza, Egypt\n\n\n7. Taj Mahal, Agra","site_name":"Joe the Cocker's Hikes","site_icon":"https://cdn.deepseek.com/site-icons/joethecockershikes.com","image_url":"https://joethecockershikeshome.files.wordpress.com/2023/11/screenshot_20231128_205543_chrome.jpg"}],"kind":"image_search"}}

